                        "documentation": " Accept the currently displayed completion candidate to the buffer.\n\n It returns false when no candidate can be accepted,\n so you can use the return value to implement a fallback:\n\n ```lua\n  vim.keymap.set('i', '<Tab>', function()\n   if not vim.lsp.inline_completion.get() then\n     return '<Tab>'\n   end\n end, { expr = true, desc = 'Accept the current inline completion' })\n ````\n\n@*return* — `true` if a completion was applied, else `false`.",
